@nsobid-646761F643AFEBB379EDD5E6A5151AF2CEF93DC1
# Metroid Dread 2.1.0 - 4:3 aspect ratio (v2.0, experimental)
# Renders at the normal 16:9 resolution with 4:3 proportions (anamorphic).
# Set the emulator's aspect ratio to "Force 4:3" or "Stretch to window".
#
# Hor- approach: all game logic (camera framing, room bounds, minimap, UI)
# still sees 16:9. Only the final perspective matrix uses aspect 4/3, so the
# vertical view matches the original and the sides are cropped.
#
# On Eden Android, don't load this as a .pchtxt/.ips: the PatchNSO copies of
# Dread's 1.8 GB image get Eden killed for low memory. Build a patched exefs
# main with scripts/make_patched_nso.py instead (see README).

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
# Camera setup for a viewport (0x1BB1CC, perspective branch). FovY is still
# computed from the 16:9 viewport; only the aspect passed to the perspective
# builder (0x79A04: m00 = cot(fovY/2) / aspect) becomes 4/3.
# 0x1BB408 mov v1.16b, v8.16b  -> ldr s1, 0x1BD654
001BB408 6112011C

# 4/3 as a float literal, in the alignment padding after the ret at 0x1BD650.
001BD654 ABAAAA3F
@stop
